= Photosynthesis — Simple =

'''Photosynthesis''' is how plants, algae and some bacteria use light to drive chemical reactions.

Many of these organisms use light energy to help turn carbon dioxide into the building blocks of sugars and other organic molecules. Plants also release oxygen as part of oxygen-producing photosynthesis.

Inside plant cells, parts of the chloroplast capture light, make energy-carrying molecules and support carbon fixation. Not every photosynthetic microorganism releases oxygen.

Photosynthesis is an important part of the [[Carbon cycle|carbon cycle]] because it moves carbon into living matter.

